From ed1bbb4526ec7647e01d692eeda720e886e02e4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ss3ds <ss3ds@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:09:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: hook 0290 upstream Frontier and battle crash fixes

Backports from upstream pspoke (pin 7477648, head 95a99b0), smallest form that fits the 3DS patch stack:

- e03aace (Battle Factory first battle jumped to 0): ov80_02236F24 passed &trainerBuf, one pointer, where
  ov80_02229F04 fills a 0x30-byte trainer record. Hook gives it the 0x30 bytes.
- 7da56e7 (Battle Hall crashed in sub_02051D18 every battle): ov80_022375D0 argument order, trainer record
  and opponent party slots fixed to match the asm.
- e1e825a (freeze when the last Pokemon faints with the foe, Self-Destruct/Explosion): BtlCmd_CalcExpGain
  returns early when nobody can take experience instead of dividing by 0.
- 7d56c81 (frozen battle animations: Water Pulse, Pin Missile, Supersonic, Fly): arg-overrides gives
  sub_02015484 (create emitter) its 3 arguments. 0262 already gave sub_020154C4 (delete) its 2.

The C edits are a hook (staged decomp, idempotent, loud on a missing anchor) so an already staged tree
gets them; only changed objects are rebuilt. The resulting code is identical to upstream's src.patch.
The arg-overrides change re-runs the translator through the existing re-sync.
